# Human review gate — the enforcement of code-standards.md §35.
#
# That section states the rule: any diff touching money, payments, pricing, or
# database policy needs human review before merge, "regardless of who or what
# wrote it". A rule stated only in prose is not a control. This file, plus a
# branch protection rule requiring code-owner review on the default branch, is
# the control.
#
# Why it exists: an agent that can weaken an RLS policy to make a test pass is a
# data-breach vector. The permission prompts in .claude/settings.json slow that
# down inside a session, but the same human who is mid-flow approving edits is
# not performing a review. Review happens on the PR, by someone accountable for
# the path.
#
# SETUP REQUIRED (cannot be done from a file):
#   1. Replace @OWNER below with the real GitHub handle or team.
#   2. Settings → Branches → protect the default branch:
#        ✔ Require a pull request before merging
#        ✔ Require review from Code Owners
#        ✔ Require status checks: typecheck, lint, test, supabase test db
#        ✔ Do not allow bypassing the above settings
#   Without step 2, this file is advisory only.

# Default — everything has an owner.
*                               @OWNER

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 High risk. A silent bug here loses real money or leaks customer PII.
#     Never self-approved. Never merged on a green build alone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ledger, Money type, idempotency, balance projections.
/lib/money/                     @OWNER

# PSP adapter and both implementations. Only the relay may call these.
/lib/psp/                       @OWNER

# Server-side price engine. Admin-configured formulas are data, never code.
/lib/pricing/                   @OWNER

# Schema, RLS policies, constraints, REVOKEs. A missing policy raises no error.
/supabase/migrations/           @OWNER

# The outbox relay — the only mutating caller of the PSP.
/supabase/functions/            @OWNER

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🟠 Controls. Changing these changes what the other gates can catch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Guardrail hooks and permission rules. Weakening a guard is a reviewable act.
/.claude/                       @OWNER

# The rules themselves, and the durable project state.
/CLAUDE.md                      @OWNER
/AGENTS.md                      @OWNER
/context/                       @OWNER

# Route protection (proxy.ts, not middleware.ts) and env validation.
/proxy.ts                       @OWNER
/lib/env.ts                     @OWNER

# Tests that prove the negative case. Deleting one is how a leak ships.
/tests/rls/                     @OWNER
/supabase/tests/                @OWNER
